  "decision_reasons": [
    "Nether aggregate throughput shifts are only 1.5\u20133.5%; all paired median ratios are within 5% of baseline. Main wins 10/20, second seed 11/20, custom 13/20, direct stem 12/20.",
    "The main-seed p95 increases from 3475 to 3846 ms; a favorable median/maximum does not erase that tail result.",
    "Overworld, which performs no version-index work in this corpus, shows a 5% throughput shift. This limits attribution of smaller Nether shifts; it does not prove the candidate cannot help under quiet conditions.",
    "Smaller live index backing does not establish lower whole-process RSS. Peaks rise for some cases; no sustained retention claim is made."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Retain all timings and recorded host observations; do not dismiss regressions as noise or declare a quiet no-regression result.",
    "The new traversal is linear in skipped newer markers. Long-history correctness is tested, but the measured six-marker maximum is not a universal performance bound.",
    "Page allocation counts exclude top-level Vec growth; backing bytes exclude allocator bookkeeping and state pointees.",
    "No concurrency/lifecycle acceptance suite is scheduled for this unselected prototype until a useful benefit is established.",
    "Observer timings and phase counters are not ordinary performance. Overworld observer before-statuses include 1 and 4; ordinary paired measurements all report status 4."
  ],
  "next": "Return to material-read attribution from the C53 CPU samples. Measure actual Owned/Shared/Cached material-call proportions and live dense-versus-RLE storage before choosing another representation. See next-material-opportunity.json; no dense representation is implemented or selected.",
